WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:33.125
<b>In the previous verse, Lord Krishna explained</b>

2
00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:36.458
<b>where and when He manifests.</b>

3
00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:43.583
<b>He descends upon this Earth when righteousness</b>
<b>declines and unrighteousness rises.</b>

4
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:50.625
<b>Now, this verse describes His purpose </b>
<b>and activities after taking avatar.</b>

5
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.250
<b>In this verse, Krishna says that</b>

6
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.583
<b>To protect His devotees,</b>

7
00:01:00.583 --> 00:01:04.375
<b>destroy the unrighteous, and establish dharma (righteousness),</b>

8
00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:06.750
<b>He takes avatar in every age.</b>

9
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.458
<b>As Krishna explained earlier,</b>

10
00:01:09.458 --> 00:01:15.166
<b>He comes when righteousness has declined</b>
<b>and unrighteousness has increased.</b>

11
00:01:15.166 --> 00:01:17.916
<b>At such times, it becomes necessary</b>

12
00:01:17.916 --> 00:01:25.083
<b>to destroy the forces spreading unrighteousness </b>
<b>and protect those who follow dharma.</b>

13
00:01:25.083 --> 00:01:26.250
<b>In this verse,</b>

14
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:31.083
<b>'devotees' refers to those who follow dharma.</b>

15
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:33.833
<b>Their protection is essential.</b>

16
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:36.291
<b>But now a question arises –</b>

17
00:01:36.291 --> 00:01:39.750
<b>why does Krishna Himself come for this task?</b>

18
00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:44.125
<b>Couldn't a righteous king have done this work?</b>

19
00:01:44.125 --> 00:01:50.416
<b>Couldn't he too have protected the dharma-</b>
<b>following devotees and destroyed the unrighteous?</b>

20
00:01:50.416 --> 00:01:52.458
<b>Yes, this is true,</b>

21
00:01:52.458 --> 00:01:53.208
<b>but</b>

22
00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:55.875
<b>there have been some unrighteous demons</b>

23
00:01:55.875 --> 00:02:01.625
<b>whose destruction wasn't possible even </b>
<b>by the most righteous kings of Earth.</b>

24
00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:04.833
<b>This task could only be </b>
<b>accomplished by Lord Krishna.</b>

25
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:07.208
<b>The slaying of Ravana in Ram's avatar,</b>

26
00:02:07.208 --> 00:02:11.083
<b>the killing of Kamsa and demon </b>
<b>Keshi in Krishna's avatar,</b>

27
00:02:11.083 --> 00:02:16.083
<b>and many such unrighteous demons required </b>
<b>Krishna's personal intervention.</b>

28
00:02:16.083 --> 00:02:20.458
<b>Moreover, there is another purpose</b>
<b>for His incarnation,</b>

29
00:02:20.458 --> 00:02:23.833
<b>which is the establishment of dharma.</b>

30
00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:27.291
<b>But naturally, a question arises –</b>

31
00:02:27.291 --> 00:02:31.333
<b>if the unrighteous are destroyed </b>
<b>and devotees are protected,</b>

32
00:02:31.333 --> 00:02:35.791
<b>wouldn't dharma be automatically established?</b>

33
00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:40.958
<b>Yes, these actions will establish </b>
<b>dharma to some extent.</b>

34
00:02:40.958 --> 00:02:41.875
<b>But</b>

35
00:02:41.875 --> 00:02:45.708
<b>there are many profound and </b>
<b>deep mysteries of dharma</b>

36
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:49.583
<b>that only Krishna can establish.</b>

37
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:51.375
<b>Understand it this way –</b>

38
00:02:51.375 --> 00:02:56.875
<b>the rivers we see don't have </b>
<b>completely transparent water,</b>

39
00:02:56.875 --> 00:03:02.875
<b>and sometimes become so impure </b>
<b>that you can't even drink from them.</b>

40
00:03:02.875 --> 00:03:07.000
<b>Was the water impure at its source?</b>

41
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.250
<b>No, right?</b>

42
00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.416
<b>The source provided pure, transparent water,</b>

43
00:03:11.416 --> 00:03:12.208
<b>but</b>

44
00:03:12.208 --> 00:03:19.833
<b>as it flowed through mountains, kingdoms, </b>
<b>and cities over time, the river became impure.</b>

45
00:03:19.833 --> 00:03:20.958
<b>Similarly,</b>

46
00:03:20.958 --> 00:03:26.000
<b>the purity of knowledge from </b>
<b>the main source is incomparable.</b>

47
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.583
<b>Like this Gita,</b>

48
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:31.583
<b>whose knowledge Krishna Himself </b>
<b>gave to Sun God Vivasvan,</b>

49
00:03:31.583 --> 00:03:36.000
<b>and then through Manu, it reached mankind.</b>

50
00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.125
<b>Yet, with time, this knowledge became clouded.</b>

51
00:03:40.125 --> 00:03:45.041
<b>And for this reason, to re-establish </b>
<b>the pure form of this knowledge,</b>

52
00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:49.916
<b>the main source itself </b>
<b>- Lord Krishna - had to come.</b>

53
00:03:49.916 --> 00:03:54.375
<b>Now you might say this knowledge will </b>
<b>again become clouded with time.</b>

54
00:03:54.375 --> 00:03:55.750
<b>And you'd be right.</b>

55
00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:58.333
<b>That's why Krishna says</b>

56
00:03:58.333 --> 00:04:02.916
<b>He takes avatar not once, but in every age,</b>

57
00:04:02.916 --> 00:04:06.541
<b>and this process will continue.</b>

58
00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:10.500
<b>Krishna will come whenever </b>
<b>unrighteousness increases,</b>

59
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.750
<b>righteousness decreases,</b>

60
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:18.500
<b>and whenever the original source is needed to </b>
<b>re-establish this knowledge of the Gita,</b>

61
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:22.000
<b>Krishna will unfailingly return..</b>

62
00:04:26.875 --> 00:04:29.291
<b>Destroying unrighteousness</b>

63
00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:32.875
<b>and establishing dharma – </b>

64
00:04:32.875 --> 00:04:40.458
<b>these are my two main purposes </b>
<b>for manifesting on Earth.</b>

65
00:04:40.458 --> 00:04:45.833
<b>And whenever the scale </b>
<b>tips towards unrighteousness,</b>

66
00:04:45.833 --> 00:04:49.041
<b>I shall come.</b>

67
00:04:49.041 --> 00:04:57.291
<b>You can apply this same principle </b>
<b>and thinking in your personal life.</b>

68
00:04:57.291 --> 00:05:01.125
<b>Your mind is like this world itself.</b>

69
00:05:01.125 --> 00:05:05.541
<b>Where some tendencies incline </b>
<b>towards unrighteousness,</b>

70
00:05:05.541 --> 00:05:14.041
<b>there also sits a sage within this mind who walks </b>
<b>the path of truth and dharma.</b>

71
00:05:14.041 --> 00:05:15.833
<b>Think about it –</b>

72
00:05:15.833 --> 00:05:20.541
<b>do I curse the world for its unrighteousness?</b>

73
00:05:20.541 --> 00:05:22.541
<b>No, right?</b>

74
00:05:22.541 --> 00:05:29.208
<b>It's simply a truth that unrighteousness </b>
<b>will exist in the world,</b>

75
00:05:29.208 --> 00:05:35.125
<b>and this doesn't make the entire world evil.</b>

76
00:05:35.125 --> 00:05:38.750
<b>So cursing it would be futile.</b>

77
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:46.916
<b>What's important is protecting the </b>
<b>sages and destroying the demons.</b>

78
00:05:46.916 --> 00:05:48.500
<b>Similarly,</b>

79
00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:51.166
<b>don't curse yourself –</b>

80
00:05:51.166 --> 00:06:01.416
<b>just strive to keep the sage within your mind safe </b>
<b>and destroy the demon within.</b>

81
00:06:01.416 --> 00:06:04.958
<b>What is your mind's sage?</b>

82
00:06:04.958 --> 00:06:08.083
<b>These are your virtues –</b>

83
00:06:08.083 --> 00:06:10.666
<b>desire for human welfare,</b>

84
00:06:10.666 --> 00:06:17.000
<b>desire for human welfare, tendency to</b>
<b>help others, compassion, truthfulness, kindness... </b>

85
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:22.333
<b>protect all these and nurture them.</b>

86
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:26.000
<b>And your mind's unrighteous demons are</b>

87
00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.416
<b>jealousy,</b>

88
00:06:27.416 --> 00:06:28.708
<b>lust,</b>

89
00:06:28.708 --> 00:06:30.125
<b>hatred.</b>

90
00:06:30.125 --> 00:06:32.375
<b>These must be destroyed.</b>

91
00:06:32.375 --> 00:06:37.375
<b>You can also see yourself as a gardener</b>

92
00:06:37.375 --> 00:06:46.291
<b>who must water the flowering plants while </b>
<b>uprooting the harmful weeds.</b>

93
00:06:46.291 --> 00:06:47.333
<b>But</b>

94
00:06:47.333 --> 00:06:50.958
<b>a gardener can only do this</b>

95
00:06:50.958 --> 00:06:57.791
<b>when they know the difference between </b>
<b>flowering and harmful plants.</b>

96
00:06:57.791 --> 00:06:58.875
<b>And</b>

97
00:06:58.875 --> 00:07:05.875
<b>I know that sometimes you must</b>
<b>find yourself in dilemmas,</b>

98
00:07:05.875 --> 00:07:13.000
<b>unable to determine which decision</b>
<b>is righteous, which unrighteous,</b>

99
00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:15.583
<b>which plant will flower</b>

100
00:07:15.583 --> 00:07:18.708
<b>and which will harm.</b>

101
00:07:18.708 --> 00:07:20.458
<b>Don't worry,</b>

102
00:07:20.458 --> 00:07:27.000
<b>as you read this Gita, all doubts </b>
<b>in your mind will clear away.</b>

103
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:30.625
<b>For now, just keep in mind –</b>

104
00:07:30.625 --> 00:07:37.250
<b>are any of your actions causing harm to society?</b>

105
00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:45.375
<b>Your decisions should benefit not just </b>
<b>you personally, but also those around you.</b>

106
00:07:45.375 --> 00:07:47.041
<b>For example,</b>

107
00:07:47.041 --> 00:07:49.083
<b>if you have an unrighteous friend</b>

108
00:07:49.083 --> 00:07:51.833
<b>who won't harm you</b>

109
00:07:51.833 --> 00:07:52.625
<b>but</b>

110
00:07:52.625 --> 00:07:57.625
<b>supporting them would harm others,</b>

111
00:07:57.625 --> 00:08:01.416
<b>then supporting them would be unrighteous</b>

112
00:08:01.416 --> 00:08:02.208
<b>and</b>

113
00:08:02.208 --> 00:08:06.416
<b>you cannot participate in this.</b>

114
00:08:06.416 --> 00:08:08.500
<b>Stay with me,</b>

115
00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:10.416
<b>I know</b>

116
00:08:10.416 --> 00:08:14.791
<b>many questions and dilemmas </b>
<b>remain to be raised in your mind,</b>

117
00:08:14.791 --> 00:08:18.000
<b>and all will be resolved.</b>

118
00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:19.291
<b>Yes,</b>

119
00:08:19.291 --> 00:08:23.291
<b>but if you're reading this Gita,</b>

120
00:08:23.291 --> 00:08:28.458
<b>then somewhere your purpose too is simply this –</b>

121
00:08:28.458 --> 00:08:32.666
<b>that the sage within your mind </b>
<b>always remains protected</b>

122
00:08:32.666 --> 00:08:36.541
<b>and no demon survives.</b>

123
00:08:41.083 --> 00:08:45.000
<b>It's natural for times to come in this world</b>

124
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:50.375
<b>when righteousness declines </b>
<b>and unrighteousness rises.</b>

125
00:08:50.375 --> 00:08:52.500
<b>Similarly,</b>

126
00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:57.125
<b>in family settings too, there come times</b>

127
00:08:57.125 --> 00:09:01.291
<b>when peace and harmony are disrupted, </b>

128
00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:05.916
<b>and discord and unrest begin to grow.</b>

129
00:09:05.916 --> 00:09:13.375
<b>This is natural when people of different</b>
<b>ages and temperaments live together.</b>

130
00:09:13.375 --> 00:09:16.958
<b>So what can be done in such a situation?</b>

131
00:09:16.958 --> 00:09:23.583
<b>You too can play Krishna's role in your family – </b>

132
00:09:23.583 --> 00:09:31.916
<b>supporting goodness and </b>
<b>preventing negativity in such times.</b>

133
00:09:31.916 --> 00:09:39.583
<b>Create an environment in your </b>
<b>family where virtues are encouraged.</b>

134
00:09:39.583 --> 00:09:42.666
<b>There are many ways to do this.</b>

135
00:09:42.666 --> 00:09:51.666
<b>The family can spend time together </b>
<b>discussing morality and proper life values.</b>

136
00:09:51.666 --> 00:09:53.750
<b>For example,</b>

137
00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:57.500
<b>everyone can share incidents</b>

138
00:09:57.500 --> 00:10:03.958
<b>when they selflessly helped a person or creature –</b>

139
00:10:03.958 --> 00:10:07.375
<b>such actions should be praised.</b>

140
00:10:07.375 --> 00:10:12.208
<b>Share religious teachings or stories</b>

141
00:10:12.208 --> 00:10:19.208
<b>that leave an impression of goodness </b>
<b>on everyone, especially youth and children.</b>

142
00:10:19.208 --> 00:10:25.791
<b>When these discussions happen regularly, </b>
<b>they begin to take root in family members' minds.</b>

143
00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:31.125
<b>And once an attraction towards </b>
<b>spirituality develops in the mind,</b>

144
00:10:31.125 --> 00:10:38.875
<b>all family members will naturally</b>
<b>be inspired to walk the path of dharma.</b>

145
00:10:38.875 --> 00:10:47.791
<b>But just as I need not only to protect the </b>
<b>virtuous but also destroy the unrighteous,</b>

146
00:10:47.791 --> 00:10:49.041
<b>similarly</b>

147
00:10:49.041 --> 00:10:54.833
<b>in family life, along with encouraging goodness,</b>

148
00:10:54.833 --> 00:10:59.541
<b>it's also necessary to protect family </b>
<b>members from negative tendencies.</b>

149
00:10:59.541 --> 00:11:00.625
<b>For this,</b>

150
00:11:00.625 --> 00:11:05.458
<b>sometimes family elders may need to be firm.</b>

151
00:11:05.458 --> 00:11:07.416
<b>Boundaries must be set,</b>

152
00:11:07.416 --> 00:11:10.000
<b>some rules established.</b>

153
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.041
<b>For example,</b>

154
00:11:12.041 --> 00:11:14.500
<b>respect for all is essential,</b>

155
00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:21.666
<b>and if someone is found being disrespectful, </b>
<b>guiding them becomes necessary.</b>

156
00:11:21.666 --> 00:11:24.041
<b>Or for instance,</b>

157
00:11:24.041 --> 00:11:33.375
<b>if a child in the family is found causing emotional </b>
<b>or physical pain to weaker classmates at school,</b>

158
00:11:33.375 --> 00:11:38.416
<b>that child should also </b>
<b>be guided towards atonement.</b>

159
00:11:38.416 --> 00:11:46.625
<b>Encouraging goodness and discouraging evil - </b>
<b>Both paths should be adopted.</b>

160
00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:48.250
<b>And yes,</b>

161
00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:54.083
<b>whether establishing dharma </b>
<b>or preventing adharma,</b>

162
00:11:54.083 --> 00:12:01.625
<b>my emotional state is solely love for humanity.</b>

163
00:12:01.625 --> 00:12:02.958
<b>Similarly,</b>

164
00:12:02.958 --> 00:12:09.208
<b>you must do all this from a </b>
<b>perspective of love and welfare,</b>

165
00:12:09.208 --> 00:12:14.416
<b>not to maintain control and</b>
<b>authority over the family.</b>

166
00:12:14.416 --> 00:12:18.375
<b>The reins of the world are in my hands;</b>

167
00:12:18.375 --> 00:12:19.333
<b>you</b>

168
00:12:19.333 --> 00:12:24.750
<b>take the reins of family guidance in yours.</b>

169
00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:28.833
<b>Share love and virtues in the family,</b>

170
00:12:28.833 --> 00:12:34.416
<b>and protect yourself and others from vices.</b>

171
00:12:39.333 --> 00:12:43.125
<b>When I manifest on Earth,</b>

172
00:12:43.125 --> 00:12:49.625
<b>my duty is to protect all those </b>
<b>who walk the path of dharma,</b>

173
00:12:49.625 --> 00:12:56.916
<b>and simultaneously, I must also punish </b>
<b>those who support evil.</b>

174
00:12:56.916 --> 00:13:06.125
<b>The only purpose is to maintain an </b>
<b>atmosphere of dharma and justice in the world.</b>

175
00:13:06.125 --> 00:13:12.791
<b>In your organization too, such a just </b>
<b>atmosphere must be maintained.</b>

176
00:13:12.791 --> 00:13:18.416
<b>An environment where everyone</b>
<b>respects each other,</b>

177
00:13:18.416 --> 00:13:22.333
<b>all colleagues walk the path of ethics, </b>

178
00:13:22.333 --> 00:13:26.208
<b>and always stay away from unethical actions.</b>

179
00:13:26.208 --> 00:13:33.250
<b>Creating such an atmosphere is the </b>
<b>most important part of leadership.</b>

180
00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:37.333
<b>For this, you must adopt both paths –</b>

181
00:13:37.333 --> 00:13:38.708
<b>where on one hand</b>

182
00:13:38.708 --> 00:13:45.958
<b>you must praise and encourage </b>
<b>colleagues who uphold organizational values,</b>

183
00:13:45.958 --> 00:13:46.958
<b>On the other hand,</b>

184
00:13:46.958 --> 00:13:50.250
<b>if someone is found breaking discipline,</b>

185
00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:55.375
<b>or conducting unethical acts for personal gain,</b>

186
00:13:55.375 --> 00:13:58.458
<b>punishing them becomes necessary.</b>

187
00:13:58.458 --> 00:13:59.541
<b>Yes,</b>

188
00:13:59.541 --> 00:14:08.083
<b>this won't be easy, because personally you </b>
<b>have affection for everyone,</b>

189
00:14:08.083 --> 00:14:09.583
<b>but remember,</b>

190
00:14:09.583 --> 00:14:15.375
<b>just as maintaining goodness in </b>
<b>this world is essential for me,</b>

191
00:14:15.375 --> 00:14:17.208
<b>similarly,</b>

192
00:14:17.208 --> 00:14:21.083
<b>organizational goals are essential for you.</b>

193
00:14:21.083 --> 00:14:28.625
<b>Don't hesitate to first show the right path to those </b>
<b>who go against organizational goals,</b>

194
00:14:28.625 --> 00:14:35.625
<b>and if there's no improvement, </b>
<b>take disciplinary action.</b>

195
00:14:35.625 --> 00:14:36.791
<b>But,</b>

196
00:14:36.791 --> 00:14:39.041
<b>do remember this –</b>

197
00:14:39.041 --> 00:14:45.375
<b>keep your mind pure, and take any </b>
<b>decision not because of personal hatred,</b>

198
00:14:45.375 --> 00:14:46.291
<b>but</b>

199
00:14:46.291 --> 00:14:52.458
<b>solely keeping in mind organizational</b>
<b>values and goals.</b>

200
00:14:52.458 --> 00:14:56.041
<b>And I also know that</b>

201
00:14:56.041 --> 00:15:00.416
<b>being in a leadership position isn't easy.</b>

202
00:15:00.416 --> 00:15:06.750
<b>I myself who am leading this entire universe.</b>

203
00:15:06.750 --> 00:15:08.583
<b>Don't worry,</b>

204
00:15:08.583 --> 00:15:11.250
<b>whenever you get caught in dilemmas,</b>

205
00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:15.958
<b>remember me, read this Gita,</b>

206
00:15:15.958 --> 00:15:20.041
<b>and the right path will surely </b>
<b>become visible to you.</b>

